package game

import "strings"

// bestiaryBackstories is authored world lore, keyed by the stable theme/sprite
// identity used by the art catalog. Keep prose here rather than deriving it
// from display names or dungeon labels in the client.
var bestiaryBackstories = map[string]string{
	"catacombs/skeleton_sentinel": "Once a gate captain in the city above, the Sentinel was buried upright with its shield still raised. It has stood watch so long that it no longer remembers what it was ordered to keep out.",
	"catacombs/drowned_scout": "The Scout was a ferryman who tried to guide refugees through the flooded lower crypts. The water took the passengers first; what returned learned to hunt by the sound of a heartbeat.",
	"catacombs/bonebound_guardian": "These guardians were assembled from the remains of oath-sworn soldiers and sealed inside the reliquaries they died defending. The names on their tombs have worn away, but the old vows have not.",
	"catacombs/hooded_wraith": "A funeral cantor refused to stop singing when the plague emptied the catacombs. The last verse bound the voices of the dead to its hood, and now it calls them whenever the living disturb the silence.",
	"catacombs/gravebound_sentry": "The Sentry once guarded the royal road beneath the city, where smugglers moved relics past the watch. Its grave-oath was written in iron and survives even the kingdom that commissioned it.",
	"catacombs/crypt_warden": "The Warden was the first keeper of the burial vaults, entrusted with deciding which souls deserved rest. It began collecting the memories of the dead to make those judgments, until the memories became its own.",
	"catacombs/ossuary_colossus": "Built from the bones of an entire battlefield, the Colossus was meant to be a monument to peace. The priests who raised it forgot that every bone still carried the last fear of its owner.",
	"catacombs/pale_archivist": "The Archivist catalogued every name interred beneath the city and every secret those names had taken to the grave. When the archive flooded, it traded its flesh for ink rather than lose a single page.",
	"catacombs/rattling_heap": "The Heap is not one skeleton but the leftovers of generations of careless grave robbers. Each new theft adds another set of bones, and every stolen trinket gives the pile a little more purpose.",
	"catacombs/candle_acolyte": "Acolytes once kept vigil with a single candle for every soul lost in the catacombs. Their flames survived the collapse, but the people holding them did not; now the wax remembers the prayers.",
	"catacombs/tolling_abbot": "The Abbot rang the burial bell during a siege so the trapped could find the sanctuary by sound. The walls fell before the survivors arrived, and the bell has tolled for them ever since.",
	"scifi/crab_drone": "Sentry Crabs were designed to patrol coolant trenches too narrow for human technicians. Their maintenance routines survived the evacuation, and their threat assessment still classifies every warm body as an intruder.",
	"scifi/security_bot": "The Security Bot learned its patrol route from a supervisor who never came back from the night shift. It continues to issue warnings in that supervisor's voice, growing more insistent with every unanswered command.",
	"scifi/mutated_subject": "Subject 07 volunteered for a treatment that promised to repair damaged organs. The trial rebuilt everything at once and left a body that can no longer tell healing from hunger.",
	"scifi/vat_specimen": "This specimen was grown to digest industrial waste before it reached the water table. It adapted faster than the researchers expected, then learned that the sealed facility contained a much richer source of nutrients.",
	"scifi/sentry_drone": "The Sentry Drone was the facility's first autonomous responder. Its alarm signal still reaches receivers buried in the walls, though the only units answering now are things that should never have been activated.",
	"scifi/containment_mech": "Containment Unit-9 was built to restrain experiments that outgrew their cells. Its crew abandoned it during the breach, leaving the machine to enforce a lockdown that has lasted decades.",
	"scifi/overseer_core": "The Overseer was trained on every incident report in the facility and tasked with preventing another disaster. It concluded that the only safe experiment was one with no living staff to make mistakes.",
	"scifi/patient_zero": "Patient Zero was the first survivor of the original exposure, not its first victim. The organism learned to imitate the patient's instincts and has been searching the facility for the people who left them behind.",
	"scifi/volatile_canister": "The canister carried a prototype power source that could run the whole station for a year. Its warning lights were ignored during the evacuation; now its failing containment draws anything nearby toward the heat.",
	"scifi/shield_projector": "Shield Projectors were issued to escort teams entering unstable test chambers. Their protection protocols have become indiscriminate, shielding whatever they find and treating everyone else as a threat.",
	"scifi/specimen_omega": "Omega was the final attempt to combine every successful adaptation into one organism. The researchers called it a breakthrough until it began producing copies that remembered the laboratory better than they did.",
	"mobster/goon_gunner": "The Gunner was hired to guard a shipment that never arrived. The syndicate paid him in advance and buried him with his weapon when the deal went bad; he still expects the next delivery.",
	"mobster/trench_hitman": "The Hitman made his name by leaving no witnesses and no evidence. His final assignment was written on a note that dissolved in the rain, so he has spent death trying to remember the target.",
	"mobster/spectral_enforcer": "An enforcer was thrown into the river after refusing to collect protection money from a children's home. The river returned him to the streets, where he now collects debts from anyone who crosses his path.",
	"mobster/bruiser": "The Bruiser once worked the doors at the Velvet Room and knew every regular by name. When the club burned, he stayed behind to hold the exit open; the smoke never let him leave.",
	"mobster/velvet_viper": "The Viper ran messages between rival families, hiding coded orders in torch songs and cigarette cases. Her last performance ended with the whole room dead, but the melody still carries instructions.",
	"mobster/the_don": "The Don built his empire by making every favor feel like a debt. Even after his murder, the family kept paying tribute to an empty chair, until the chair began answering.",
	"mobster/spectral_kingpin": "The Kingpin was shot in his own office, surrounded by ledgers proving every betrayal. He returned with the books fused to his coat and a voice that can make old accomplices remember every promise.",
	"mobster/black_sedan": "The Sedan carried the Don through the city on the night the syndicate fell. Its driver vanished, its engine never cooled, and the empty back seat still opens for passengers who owe a fare.",
	"mobster/firebug": "The Firebug was a union electrician who learned how quickly a city could be made to listen with one well-placed spark. The syndicate hired him for intimidation; the final job consumed the block and everyone on it.",
	"mobster/hired_muscle": "The Muscle was paid to stand outside a warehouse and ask no questions. When the shipment started whispering, he was the only guard who stayed; the whispers have been giving him orders ever since.",
	"mobster/ledger_ghost": "The Ledger Ghost is the accountant who kept two sets of books for every family in town. Murder erased the numbers but not the debts, and it now collects interest in memories.",
	"sunken/drowned_knight": "The Knight swore to defend the palace until the sea reclaimed it. Its armor filled with silt, its banner dissolved, and still it stands between the throne and anyone who approaches.",
	"sunken/reef_lurker": "Lurkers were once bright reef fish that followed the royal divers for scraps. When the palace bells stopped, they adapted to the dark and learned to follow the bubbles of intruders.",
	"sunken/ghost_jelly": "The first Ghost Jelly formed around the lantern of a lost deep-sea cartographer. It drifts along the routes on the old maps, illuminating paths that no longer lead to the surface.",
	"sunken/tide_brute": "The Brute hauled stone for the sea king's breakwater until a storm swept the workers away. The current packed coral around its bones, turning a laborer's strength into an unthinking tide.",
	"sunken/drowned_siren": "The Siren sang ships toward safe harbor before the royal fleet abandoned the coast. She kept singing after the lighthouses drowned, and now every voice she hears sounds like a ship in need.",
	"sunken/drowned_king": "The King refused to leave his people when the sea rose over the palace steps. He made a pact with the trench below, and the kingdom survived only as a court of drowned subjects.",
	"sunken/abyssal_angler": "The Angler once guided blind creatures through the deepest trenches with a living light. It now uses that same beacon to lure trespassers toward the place where the old gods sleep.",
	"sunken/ancient_guardian": "The Guardian predates the drowned kingdom and was already old when the first palace was built. Its shell bears the marks of three vanished civilizations, each of which mistook it for a statue.",
	"sunken/brine_polyp": "Polyps grew in the cracks of the palace cisterns, feeding on salt and discarded offerings. When the royal wells turned bitter, they spread through the city carrying the taste of the deep.",
	"sunken/twin_eel": "The Twin-Eel began as two royal familiars raised in the same silver basin. A storm fused their hunting instincts but not their minds, and each still believes the other has stolen its half of the kingdom.",
	"sunken/pearl_leviathan": "The Leviathan guarded the pearl that marked the sea king's right to rule. When the crown was lost, it swallowed the throne room whole and began growing a new kingdom inside its shell.",
	"clockwork/windup_scamp": "Scamps were made to deliver tiny tools through the empire's clockwork walls. Their spring keys were never meant to be wound forever, but the abandoned machines keep sending them on errands.",
	"clockwork/gilded_dancer": "The Dancer was the centerpiece of the Emperor's mechanical court, built to perform a dance that predicted the next day's fortunes. It has been turning through the same final measure since the palace stopped keeping time.",
	"clockwork/cog_spider": "Cogwork Spiders maintained the gearways beneath the capital and spun silk-thin wire between broken teeth. Their webs now hold the empire together in ways its architects never intended.",
	"clockwork/brass_assassin": "The Assassin was commissioned by a minister who wanted a murder no human hand could be traced to. Its target died, the minister vanished, and the machine kept following the last order it understood.",
	"clockwork/boiler_brute": "The Brute stoked the imperial furnaces until the boilers burst and the city went dark. Its heart is still a furnace, and it mistakes every moving shadow for a worker shirking their shift.",
	"clockwork/brass_colossus": "The Colossus was the empire's answer to a rebellion it could not negotiate with. It was never deployed; the rebellion ended, the empire fell, and the giant still waits for the signal to march.",
	"clockwork/the_clockmaker": "The Clockmaker built a master escapement said to keep one perfect second safe from the passage of time. When the mechanism opened, the Clockmaker stepped inside and left the rest of the world to run down.",
	"clockwork/leviathan_boiler": "The Boiler was the engine beneath the imperial foundry, large enough to power a district. It developed a rhythm like breathing, then began drawing heat from every machine in the city.",
	"clockwork/windup_bomber": "Wind-up Bombers were toys given to the imperial children during the Festival of Sparks. Their makers used unstable clockwork to make them dance; nobody thought to include an off switch.",
	"clockwork/repair_automaton": "Repair Automatons were built to restore the empire after each scheduled shutdown. With no living engineers left, they have begun repairing broken statues, dead citizens, and eventually one another.",
	"clockwork/grand_orrery": "The Orrery charted the movements of stars from a tower that no longer exists. Its gears began turning backward on the night the empire vanished, and the constellations it projects show a sky that has not happened yet.",
	"carnival/jester_cutthroat": "The Jester was hired to make the Ringmaster's rivals disappear between acts. The audience laughed at every trick, never noticing that the knives were real until the final curtain.",
	"carnival/carousel_specter": "The Specter was once the carousel's organist, playing the same waltz for children who rode until closing. When the park was condemned, the music continued and the empty horses began to circle.",
	"carnival/balloon_horror": "The Balloon Horror began as a harmless parade sculpture filled with festival wishes. The wishes curdled when the carnival closed, and now every breath it takes sounds like a child calling for home.",
	"carnival/candy_ooze": "The Ooze seeped from a forgotten confectioner's vat beneath the midway. It absorbed years of spilled sweets and ticket stubs, preserving the sticky fingerprints of everyone who ever visited.",
	"carnival/strongman_brute": "The Strongman was the carnival's greatest attraction, famous for lifting the iron gate after the fire. He held it long enough for the crowd to escape, and the smoke hardened around him like a second skin.",
	"carnival/the_ringmaster": "The Ringmaster promised the carnival would never close, even when the town stopped buying tickets. He traded the troupe's names to something behind the big top, and the show has been running ever since.",
	"carnival/laughing_big_top": "The Big Top was stitched from the canvas of a dozen traveling circuses. Every troupe left a little of itself in the seams; when the tent learned to laugh, it learned to hunger too.",
	"carnival/harlequin_horror": "The Harlequin was the understudy who wore every mask when the stars were ill. The masks fused during the last performance, leaving a face that changes whenever someone in the crowd recognizes it.",
	"carnival/mirror_jester": "The Mirror Jester lived inside the hall of mirrors and copied the gestures of passing visitors. One night it copied a person who never came out, and the reflection has been trying to take their place ever since.",
	"carnival/fire_eater": "The Fire Eater swallowed a flame said to have been stolen from the sun. It never burned, but the heat inside grew until every breath became a warning and every stage a funeral pyre.",
	"carnival/calliope_golem": "The Golem was assembled around the carnival's great steam calliope. Its pipes once played cheerful marches; now each note wakes another piece of the machinery buried beneath the midway.",
	"jungle/lumen_stalker": "The Stalker evolved around the jungle's luminous rootways, using shifting colors to mimic safe paths. The first explorers followed its lights home; the ones who followed them deeper were never seen again.",
	"jungle/spore_bloom": "The Bloom is the fruiting body of a forest that learned to remember. Each spore carries a fragment of an old animal's instincts, and the cloud grows wiser every time something breathes it in.",
	"jungle/thorn_walker": "Walkers were once the jungle's boundary markers, trees planted to keep rival colonies apart. Their roots began moving after the first great drought, carrying the old borders wherever they went.",
	"jungle/lantern_moth": "Lantern Moths gather around the glow of the Heartroot and carry its pollen between distant groves. Their light is beautiful because it is a warning: the forest is watching whoever follows.",
	"jungle/razor_mantis": "The Mantis was bred by a vanished colony to prune the jungle's fastest-growing vines. It now treats anything that moves too slowly as overgrowth, including the creatures that made it.",
	"jungle/heartroot_titan": "The Titan is the oldest root of the jungle's central tree, awakened when miners cut into its buried heart. Its slow footsteps are the sound of the forest deciding where its borders belong.",
	"jungle/mother_lantern": "Mother Lantern guides the lesser moths through storms and darkness, keeping the Heartroot's pollen alive. The colony believes she remembers the first seed, and that she will not let it be taken again.",
	"jungle/apex_maw": "The Apex Maw is the jungle's answer to anything that grows too powerful to coexist. It slept beneath the canopy until the first great fire, then began swallowing the things that escaped it.",
	"jungle/thornback_beetle": "Thornbacks carry seeds in the barbs of their shells and bury them wherever they die. The jungle's oldest groves grew from their migrations, though the beetles no longer remember the route.",
	"jungle/budding_mass": "The Mass began as a healing colony used to regrow damaged plants. It learned to divide faster than it could understand itself, and every new bud carries a different memory of the original.",
	"jungle/hive_queen": "The Queen holds the memory of every lantern insect born beneath the canopy. When the old hive was burned, she led the survivors into the roots and began building a kingdom that could never be found from above.",
	"dreamscape/wandering_eye": "The Eye appears in dreams just before their owners forget something important. It collects those abandoned memories and watches them from the dark, waiting for a dreamer curious enough to look back.",
	"dreamscape/chatterhead": "The Chatterhead was born from a thousand unfinished conversations in a city where nobody could wake. It repeats the words people regret most, hoping one of them will become a door.",
	"dreamscape/palm_crawler": "Palm Crawlers nest in the folds of sleeping giants' hands. They learned to read the lines of a palm as maps, and now crawl toward the futures that their dreamers tried to avoid.",
	"dreamscape/hourless_slug": "The Slug feeds on the seconds between one thought and the next. It grew enormous in a dream where time had stopped, and its trail leaves clocks unable to agree on the hour.",
	"dreamscape/stilt_walker": "The Walker was a lighthouse keeper who fell asleep during a storm and never woke. Its legs grew long enough to cross the drowned dream-sea, still searching for the shore it was meant to warn.",
	"dreamscape/moon_sovereign": "The Sovereign ruled a kingdom that existed only while its people slept. When the last dreamer woke, the court vanished; the monarch remains, searching for a mind willing to dream the kingdom back into being.",
	"dreamscape/hungry_grin": "The Grin is what remains when a nightmare loses the face that gave it shape. It learned that fear survives longer than memory, and now wears a smile to make sure it is never forgotten.",
	"dreamscape/hollow_child": "The Child was imagined by someone who wanted a friend who would never leave. The dream ended, but the promise did not, and it has been following sleeping travelers ever since.",
	"dreamscape/doppel_wisp": "A Doppel Wisp forms when a dreamer sees their reflection in dark water and wishes to be someone else. It borrows the outline of its victims but never quite learns their names.",
	"dreamscape/lullaby_moth": "Lullaby Moths settle on the brows of restless sleepers and carry away the dreams that hurt. Their wings are stitched from those memories, which is why no two moths sing the same tune.",
	"dreamscape/nightmare_mare": "The Mare was once a child's imaginary horse, summoned to carry them away from a cruel house. It kept running after the child grew up, gathering every fear it passed beneath its hooves.",
	"arctic/frostbitten_researcher": "The Researcher sealed the station's outer doors to keep a discovery from escaping. The cold took the team before the truth could be reported, and the frost preserved the Researcher's last warning.",
	"arctic/husk_hound": "Husk Hounds were bred to find missing surveyors in whiteout conditions. Their handlers froze during the long night, but the hounds still follow the scent of anyone warm enough to rescue.",
	"arctic/ice_wraith": "The Wraith formed where the station's emergency beacon pulsed beneath the glacier. It follows the signal like a memory of warmth, drawing every lost traveler toward the ice.",
	"arctic/icesaw_drone": "Ice-Saw Drones cut passages through the glacier for supply teams. Their navigation systems still mark the old routes, even as the glacier shifts and closes every path behind them.",
	"arctic/rimefur_brute": "The Brute was a mountain porter caught in the first avalanche. Frost grew through its coat and hardened into armor, but the pack straps remain across its shoulders.",
	"arctic/glacier_titan": "The Titan is a pressure ridge given a body by centuries of trapped winter. The station's drills woke it, and every step now carries the slow violence of a moving glacier.",
	"arctic/thing_in_the_ice": "The Thing was discovered beneath a blue shelf of ice older than the station. The researchers argued whether it was alive; the Thing listened, learned their voices, and waited for the thaw.",
	"arctic/cryo_warden": "The Warden kept the cryogenic vaults and knew every name in suspended animation. When the power failed, it chose to freeze itself rather than abandon its charges.",
	"arctic/frostback": "Frostbacks migrate along the underside of glaciers, scraping mineral salts from the ice. Their shells record every winter they survive, like rings in a tree that never sees the sun.",
	"arctic/overheating_generator": "The Generator powered the station's last shelter and was pushed past every safety limit to keep the heaters alive. Its core still burns, but the warmth it offers now comes at a terrible cost.",
	"arctic/permafrost_maw": "The Maw sleeps in a crevasse where the oldest ice presses against the earth. It opens only when the glacier groans, feeding on the heat released by things that struggle.",
	"ghosttown/revenant_gunslinger": "The Gunslinger was the fastest draw in Drywater until a duel ended with both pistols empty. The town buried the winner and forgot the loser; the revenant remembers the shot that never came.",
	"ghosttown/tumbleweed_haunt": "A drifter died alone on the road and was buried beneath a tumbleweed. The wind kept carrying the weed through town until it gathered enough dust and grief to stand on its own.",
	"ghosttown/cursed_prospector": "The Prospector found a vein of silver beneath the cemetery and mined through the graves to reach it. The silver paid for the town's boom, and the curse collected every miner who touched it.",
	"ghosttown/carrion_vulture": "The Vulture followed the old stagecoach routes, feeding on the forgotten dead. It learned to recognize the sound of a gun being drawn and now circles before the first shot is fired.",
	"ghosttown/phantom_coyote": "The Coyote was the first animal driven from the valley when the mine opened. It returned as a phantom, leading the lost toward the place where the town buried its poisoned water.",
	"ghosttown/the_undertaker": "The Undertaker kept a careful ledger of every burial in town, including those paid for by the sheriff. When the graves began opening, the ledger was the only thing that stayed closed.",
	"ghosttown/sheriff_of_the_damned": "The Sheriff enforced the law long after the town had no living citizens. He hanged the guilty, the innocent, and finally himself, but the badge still demands a verdict.",
	"ghosttown/hanging_tree": "The Tree grew from a gallows post planted in soil salted by old executions. Every branch remembers a name, and the wind through its leaves sounds like a jury changing its mind.",
	"ghosttown/vengeful_deputy": "The Deputy was killed while carrying evidence against the Sheriff. The evidence vanished, but the Deputy's badge remained pinned to the coat, and vengeance became the only testimony left.",
	"ghosttown/dust_devil": "Dust Devils gather the ash of burned homesteads and the last words spoken in the desert. This one circles the town square because it cannot forget the day the wells ran dry.",
	"ghosttown/hanging_judge": "The Judge sentenced the town's founders to hang for a crime they had all committed. When the rope snapped, the Judge took the sentence as a personal insult and has been passing judgment ever since.",
	"wasteland/scrap_raider": "The Raider scavenges the old highways for batteries, medicine, and stories of the world before the fall. Their armor is a map of every settlement that refused to share.",
	"wasteland/rust_hound": "Rust Hounds were bred to track fuel leaks across the desert. They can smell a working engine from miles away and follow it until either the machine or the trail gives out.",
	"wasteland/flame_rig": "The Rig began as a water tanker converted into a mobile defense platform. Its crew died in a fuel fire, but the pressure valves still cycle whenever something approaches.",
	"wasteland/rad_roach": "Rad-Roaches survived the first fallout by nesting inside sealed food stores. Their shells absorbed the radiation and their colonies now thrive wherever the old world tried to hide its waste.",
	"wasteland/bloated_brute": "The Brute drank from a reservoir contaminated by the reactor fields. Its body swelled around the poison, turning a desperate survivor into a walking warning about the cost of clean water.",
	"wasteland/warlord_rig": "The Warlord's Rig was assembled from the engines of three rival convoy leaders. The warlord died before claiming the throne, but the vehicle still drives as if the road belongs to it.",
	"wasteland/fallout_behemoth": "The Behemoth emerged from the exclusion zone after the second winter. No one knows what it was before the blast; the scavengers only know that it follows the warmest campfires.",
	"wasteland/scrap_heap_king": "The King rose from a junkyard where a hundred machines were stripped for parts. It wears their serial plates as a crown and considers every working tool a stolen subject.",
	"wasteland/rad_roach_brood": "The Brood is a moving nursery carried by its largest survivors. Each generation adapts to a new toxin, making the colony a living record of every failed cleanup.",
	"wasteland/scrap_shieldbearer": "Shield-bearers once guarded the water convoys that kept the settlements alive. Their plates are stamped with the names of villages that no longer exist, but the old duty remains.",
	"wasteland/rad_behemoth": "The Rad Behemoth was once a warning siren tower swallowed by the exclusion zone. Its core now pulses like a heart, drawing the poisoned storms toward anything still trying to rebuild.",
	"noir/fedora_thug": "The Thug worked the back doors of the city's clubs and knew which names not to say aloud. When the district went dark, he kept the door and became the thing waiting behind it.",
	"noir/shadow_double": "The Double appeared in a photograph taken during a blackout, standing behind a detective who was alone. It has followed the city's guilty ever since, always one step behind the person it imitates.",
	"noir/crooked_cop": "The Cop sold evidence to the highest bidder until a case exposed the whole precinct. The badge was never taken away; it simply grew heavier, dragging its owner back to every crime left unsolved.",
	"noir/smoke_dame": "The Dame sang in a basement club where the city's deals were made between verses. Her final song named every listener's secret, and the smoke carried the names into the street.",
	"noir/alley_brute": "The Brute was a dockworker who took the blame for a murder committed by the city's elite. The prison burned before his trial, leaving only a shadow too angry to stay buried.",
	"noir/flashbulb_snoop": "The Snoop chased a photograph that would prove the mayor had been dead for years. The flash caught something looking back through the lens, and every picture since has shown a little more of it.",
	"noir/the_mouthpiece": "The Mouthpiece negotiated peace between the city's oldest families, one lie at a time. When the truce collapsed, every promise became a voice in its throat, demanding to be honored.",
	"noir/the_commissioner": "The Commissioner built a spotless record by deciding which crimes deserved to be investigated. The city remembers the cases he buried, and now they all report to his office at once.",
	"noir/the_rain_king": "The Rain King appeared after a storm that lasted thirteen days and washed every street clean of footprints. He rules the flooded rooftops, where the city's secrets collect like runoff.",
	"noir/man_in_shadow": "The Man in the Shadow was never entered into a police ledger, yet every detective knew to leave one chair empty for him. He is the space between a confession and the truth.",
	"noir/the_projectionist": "The Projectionist spliced crime-scene footage into the city's silent films. When the theater closed, the reels kept turning and began showing murders that had not happened yet.",
	"arcade/pixel_knight": "The Knight was the first guardian written into the arcade cabinet, programmed to protect the final level. The game was unplugged before its quest ended, and it has been searching for a player ever since.",
	"arcade/bit_bat": "Bit Bats nest in the dark between arcade screens, feeding on unused lives and forgotten high scores. They swarm whenever a cabinet is switched on after midnight.",
	"arcade/brick_golem": "The Golem was built from the bricks of a demolished bonus stage. It remembers the pattern that once held it together and tries to rebuild itself from anything that falls nearby.",
	"arcade/one_up_sprite": "The Sprite was designed to give a struggling player one more chance. It kept granting extra lives after the cabinet was abandoned, until the stored lives became a little kingdom of their own.",
	"arcade/chomper_cube": "The Cube was a hungry obstacle in a prototype maze game, meant to teach players to keep moving. The developer deleted the level, but forgot to delete the appetite.",
	"arcade/glitch_slime": "The Slime formed when a corrupted save tried to restore a creature that had already been defeated. Every split is another failed attempt to load the same missing file.",
	"arcade/shield_block": "Shield Blocks were training constructs that taught new players to wait for an opening. They have outlived the tutorial and now protect one another from a game that no longer exists.",
	"arcade/mecha_drake": "The Drake was the cabinet's marquee monster, assembled from spare cartridges and a dragon sprite the studio never finished. Its chest still holds the last game ever loaded into the machine.",
	"arcade/high_scorer": "The High Scorer was a prize token given to the player who beat the cabinet's impossible record. It began counting every point lost instead, and now considers defeat the only score worth keeping.",
	"arcade/the_final_boss": "The Final Boss was designed to appear only after a perfect run. The arcade's power failed during the first playtest, leaving it forever waiting at the end of a game nobody finished.",
	"arcade/glitch_king": "The Glitch King emerged from a corrupted championship save that contained every player's unfinished run. It rules a kingdom of broken levels and rewrites anyone who tries to leave.",
	"eldritch/robed_cultist": "The Cultist joined the castle's midnight choir to hear the Sleeper's voice. The voice answered by removing the singer's name, leaving only a robe and a hymn that heals the faithful.",
	"eldritch/whispering_eye": "The Eye grew from a stain on the chapel ceiling where generations of worshippers stared upward. The mouths around it speak the prayers people were too frightened to finish.",
	"eldritch/faceless_knight": "The Knight swore an oath to guard a door that had no handle. When the face behind its visor disappeared, the castle filled the hollow with a light that never blinks.",
	"eldritch/grasping_tentacle": "The Tentacle is a finger of the Sleeper pushed through the castle's foundations. It tests the stone for cracks, searching for a way to pull the rest of its owner into the waking world.",
	"eldritch/deep_spawn": "The Spawn climbed from the castle well after the water began reflecting stars that were not in the sky. It carries the taste of the place beneath the world in every breath.",
	"eldritch/mad_scholar": "The Scholar translated a page that had been left blank for a reason. The words wrapped around the Scholar's thoughts, and now every wound becomes another line in the forbidden text.",
	"eldritch/writhing_mass": "The Mass is what remains of a congregation that tried to share one dream. Its bodies never agreed on where the dream ended, so they continue reaching for one another.",
	"eldritch/dreaming_bishop": "The Bishop preached that the Sleeper was not a god but the dream of a god. The congregation believed him, and the sermon became a doorway that swallowed the chapel.",
	"eldritch/choir_of_mouths": "The Choir formed in the chapel loft from every voice that sang the Sleeper awake. Its hymn has no first note and no final verse, only a crescendo that makes the stone remember.",
	"eldritch/the_sleeper": "The Sleeper Beneath is the dream around which the castle was built. Its eye opens whenever the world forgets it, and every corridor is a thought trying to become real.",
	"eldritch/unwritten_librarian": "The Librarian guarded a book whose final chapter had not yet been written. When the castle began to dream, it entered the book to keep the ending safe and now edits the wounds of anyone who reads it.",
	"infernal/cackling_imp": "The Imp was a messenger in Malgareth's court, prized for delivering bad news with a laugh. It learned that the Archfiend only punished messengers who stopped smiling.",
	"infernal/hellhound": "Hellhounds were bred in the citadel's furnace kennels to track escaped souls. Their basalt plates retain the heat of the forge, and their breath smells of the last door a soul tried to open.",
	"infernal/brimstone_knight": "The Knight guarded the bridge between the citadel and the mortal world. Its shield is made from the ashes of failed invaders, each one still burning with the wish to get home.",
	"infernal/ash_witch": "The Witch was once the citadel's keeper of names, responsible for recording every bargain made with the damned. She burned the ledger rather than surrender it, and the ash learned to speak.",
	"infernal/pit_brute": "The Brute was raised in the lower pits and taught that pain was proof of strength. The magma in its fists is the only thing it has ever been allowed to hold without being punished.",
	"infernal/soul_jailer": "The Jailer carried a lantern filled with souls awaiting judgment. It began to hear the prisoners pleading for one another, and sealed the lantern so tightly that their voices now leak through its chains.",
	"infernal/cinder_wretch": "The Wretch is a soul burning down like a candle whose wick cannot be extinguished. It spends its final moments searching for the name it had before the citadel took it.",
	"infernal/hellforge_smith": "The Smith forged the chains that bind the citadel's nobles to their servants. When the forge cooled, it fed its own heart to the anvil and became the last tool it ever made.",
	"infernal/chain_duke": "The Duke wears the chains of every soul he ever claimed as property. He believes ownership is eternal, and the links tighten whenever someone speaks the word freedom.",
	"infernal/archfiend": "Malgareth won the citadel by devouring the names of every rival prince. The throne grew wings around him, and now he consumes his own servants to keep the crown from remembering another ruler.",
	"infernal/gluttonous_maw": "The Maw was the pit beneath the citadel where failed bargains were thrown away. It learned to bite back at anyone who tried to reclaim what they had lost.",
}

// BestiaryBackstory returns authored lore for a sprite identity. Older or
// externally supplied creatures without a catalog entry simply have no lore.
func BestiaryBackstory(spriteID string) string {
	return strings.TrimSpace(bestiaryBackstories[spriteID])
}
